WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:07.930
Speaker 1: Asked on Fox News why gun deaths
in the United States are so much higher than

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.709
in comparable countries, Congressman Steve
Scalise blamed the defund the police movement

00:00:13.709 --> 00:00:19.029
and unfortunately the Fox News host in question,
John Roberts, didn't even attempt to push

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:20.029
back.

00:00:20.029 --> 00:00:21.289
So there is a lot behind this.

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:28.500
And we've been talking about the the senseless
I mean, just bizarre justifications and explanations

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.010
that Republicans and the pro-gun right have
given for why we have mass shootings in the

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.510
U.S. and you don't see them in other countries.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.899
They've talked about COVID, even though every
country had covered video games doors.

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:41.699
They haven't gotten to windows yet.

00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:43.719
But maybe they will.

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:44.719
But this is a good question.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:45.719
Why?

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:46.840
Why is this a problem here?

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:52.269
And almost nowhere else, at least in terms
of Western countries here is Steve Scalise

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:53.710
attempt at explaining it.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:58.700
Speaker 3: Look, look, let me move ahead to
what's going on in this country, because in

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:04.750
terms of the developed world, the United States
far and away leads every other nation in the

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.909
developed world in terms of gun violence.

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:08.780
Speaker 1: Hey and good for Fox.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:14.870
They put up a chart showing how insanely higher
the rate of of gun violence deaths is in the

00:01:14.870 --> 00:01:16.870
U.S. than in any other country.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:18.500
Good for Fox for at least doing that.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.090
Speaker 3: Look at this graph.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.450
The U.S. way out in front with four deaths
per 100,000 people.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:32.170
The next closest nation is Cyprus, way behind
it, just below 0.7 deaths per 100 people.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:35.119
What do you think is responsible for that
discrepancy?

00:01:35.119 --> 00:01:40.610
Well, in a lot of those countries, first of
all, I mean, you look at America in the last

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:44.640
couple of years, you've seen this crazy defund
the police movement, but you've also seen

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:49.050
a movement that's been going on for a few
years in big cities where the DA's aren't

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.820
even prosecuting criminals until it is a shooting
or a violent crime.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:59.219
Speaker 1: And what what is this guy talking
about?

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:03.240
First of all, defund the police is a slogan.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.100
Almost no departments have substantially defunded
anything.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.800
Some have reallocated funds.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.520
Some have increased funding to police.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.750
But think about another thing.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:19.430
The police departments in many of those other
countries on the list are already more like

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:23.970
the police departments that the reform the
police movement wants anyway.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.060
So think about that.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.980
They're saying the defund the police movement
is responsible.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.190
It's a slogan that's accomplished almost nothing.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:35.830
But if it did, all it would do is make police
departments look more like the police departments

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:41.480
in Italy, in France, in other places where
not necessarily all officers have firearms

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.370
or you don't necessarily have an armed response
to every 911 goal.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:51.200
But the idea that there are mass shootings,
the mass shooters who they say are mentally

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:57.810
ill, are deciding whether to go and do shootings
based on what days are doing it.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.210
It's completely incoherent.

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.490
Speaker 3: Letting criminals back out on the
streets.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.730
And then inevitably what you see is higher
rates of crime.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.410
Speaker 1: And it's it's completely absurd.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:11.200
These mass shootings were not criminals that
had been left out, but left back out on the

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.200
street, let back out.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.260
Speaker 3: What you're also seeing is more
and more American citizens, law abiding citizens,

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.290
are buying guns to defend themselves.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.510
Speaker 1: But the question was, why do we
have so many shootings?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.970
And he's saying, well, all these citizens
are buying guns to defend themselves.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:29.010
He's not trying to make that point, but he's
almost inadvertently making it more guns,

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.010
makes it more dangerous.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:34.530
Speaker 3: It's happening in every demographic
group you can imagine where you have large

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:39.430
increases in people buying guns, because if
they can have faith that their local police

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.030
department that's been defunded can arrive
quickly.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.800
Speaker 1: At this this guy's disgusting.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.140
As you know, barely any any defunding has
taken place.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.950
And it's just it's a slogan.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:54.610
And blaming the epidemic of gun violence on
a slogan that, first of all, is very new.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:04:00.090
Defund the police as a as a widespread slogan,
which, by the way, almost no one on the left

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.090
supports.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.640
I mean, quite literally, almost no one, you
do polling.

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.470
Most of the left wants to reform the police.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.260
They don't want to defund it.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.260
That's what you're blaming it on.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.820
And what about all the mass shootings that
have taken place before?

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.820
That became a slogan.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.710
Now I tweeted something similar.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:14.760
How do they explain it?

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:19.360
I tweeted, quote, It would be interesting
to figure out why a country like Italy, for

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.450
example, has essentially no mass shootings.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.720
They have economic problems.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.720
They have diversity.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.940
You know, sometimes the right likes to say,
well, homogenous countries have less violence,

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.730
like countries like, you know, they often
point to.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.350
Norway or whatever.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.730
Italy is a diverse country.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:35.810
What?

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.190
But they have almost no mass shootings.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.190
What could be the reason?

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.940
And the great Betsy Brandt, who played Marie
on Breaking Bad, responded.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.790
No one knows, of course, tongue in cheek.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:45.970
The guns are the difference.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:50.910
And people jokingly responded and said, Well,
Italy has fresh pasta.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.080
Italy doesn't have doors.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.580
Of course, that's a joke.

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:59.320
But in all seriousness, Italy has doors and
they have video games and they had COVID mandates.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:04.580
They have everything other than as many guns
as we have per capita, and they don't have

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.820
toxic American gun culture.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.880
It's both things.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:14.070
So any sensible person can see it's pointing
very strongly to the guns.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.560
Deal with everything else.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.560
Sure.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.000
But you've got to deal with the guns as well.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:23.950
Now, in addition that the the pointing fingers
at the defund the police movement, you know,

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:29.180
the Uvalde, Texas PD Department, a PD police
department was well funded.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.260
And in fact, the police department there had
40% of the city's budget.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.590
So think about that.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:38.620
40% of the budget in Uvalde is police.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.970
They have everything they need to go in and
stop a shooter.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:43.960
And they stood outside for an hour.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:50.740
So at least as far as that's concerned, defund
the police are a non-factor.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.470
And Steve Scalise is doing what they all do,
just running interference.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:55.840
That's all they want to do.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.970
They're not going to stop.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.940
They don't want to deal with guns in any serious
way.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:04.370
And this is what you get, by the way, four
